<title>INDIA: India Thermax 96/97 net down.</title>
<headline>India Thermax 96/97 net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    431.6   vs    451.7</p>
<p>    Income		5,090.2   vs  4,644.1</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)     18.56   vs    19.64</p>
<p>    Other income	   76.1   vs     60.2</p>
<p>    Extraord income	58.2   vs	NIL</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 4,518.3   vs   4,006.6</p>
<p>    Interest		 84.9   vs	58.2</p>
<p>    Gross profit	  621.3   vs     639.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   89.7   vs	64.9</p>
<p>    Tax		     100.0   vs     123.0</p>
<p>Note - Thermax Ltd makes industrial boilers apart from putting up turn-key projects.</p>
<p>Operations were hit by subdued market conditions, liquidity crunch faced by clients and year-end truckers' strike, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The latest results are unaudited.</p>
<p>The company's directors did not recommend a dividend, but said the reserves at 2.67 billion rupees, against 2.23 billion a year ago, was subject to dividend provision for the year. It had paid a dividend of 3.5 rupees per 10-rupee face value stock for 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
